# Addresses and domains the release scan lets through, one per line: "address | reason".
# "*@domain" allows every address at that domain. Only reserved test domains and generic
# protocol users belong here. A real person's address does not.
*@example.com | reserved by RFC 2606, test fixtures only
*@example.test | reserved by RFC 2606, test fixtures only
*@b.example | reserved TLD, test fixtures only
*@d.example | reserved TLD, test fixtures only
*@x.test | reserved TLD, test fixtures only
git@github.com | the standard SSH user in a git remote URL, not a person
local@local.invalid | reserved TLD (RFC 2606): the fixed key name a copy kept in the page binds its locked-note and app-lock keys to, never shown or sent
